      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "title: \"Poisson Regression Examples\"\n",
        "author: \"Mariana Vejar\"\n",
        "date: today\n",
        "callout-appearance: minimal # this hides the blue \"i\" icon on .callout-notes\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Blueprinty Case Study\n",
        "\n",
        "### Introduction\n",
        "\n",
        "Blueprinty is a small firm that makes software for developing blueprints specifically for submitting patent applications to the US patent office. Their marketing team would like to make the claim that patent applicants using Blueprinty's software are more successful in getting their patent applications approved. Ideal data to study such an effect might include the success rate of patent applications before using Blueprinty's software and after using it. Unfortunately, such data is not available. \n",
        "\n",
        "However, Blueprinty has collected data on 1,500 mature (non-startup) engineering firms. The data include each firm's number of patents awarded over the last 5 years, regional location, age since incorporation, and whether or not the firm uses Blueprinty's software. The marketing team would like to use this data to make the claim that firms using Blueprinty's software are more successful in getting their patent applications approved.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "### Data"
      ],
      "id": "c7df7184"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "\n",
        "blueprinty = pd.read_csv(\"/home/jovyan/Desktop/mysite/projects/hw2/blueprinty.csv\")\n",
        "\n",
        "blueprinty.info()\n",
        "blueprinty.describe()\n",
        "\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "\n",
        "import seaborn as sns\n",
        "\n",
        "sns.set(style=\"whitegrid\")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n",
        "sns.histplot(data=blueprinty, x=\"patents\", hue=\"iscustomer\", bins=30, kde=False, multiple=\"dodge\")\n",
        "plt.title(\"Distribution of Patents by Customer Status\")\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"Number of Patents\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"Count\")\n",
        "plt.legend(title=\"Is Customer\", labels=[\"Non-Customer\", \"Customer\"])\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()\n",
        "\n",
        "blueprinty.groupby(\"iscustomer\")[\"patents\"].mean().round(2)"
      ],
      "id": "d2f52a8a",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "📊 Observations: Patents by Customer Status\n",
        "\n",
        "Average Patents:\n",
        "- Customers have a higher mean number of patents (4.13) than non-customers (3.47).\n",
        "- This supports the idea that more prolific inventors are more likely to be customers of Blueprinty.\n",
        "\n",
        "Distribution Shape:\n",
        "- Both groups show a right-skewed distribution, typical of count data.\n",
        "- Customers have noticeably higher counts in the upper range, suggesting they are overrepresented among more active inventors.\n",
        "\n",
        "Interpretation:\n",
        "- Blueprinty seems to attract customers with more patents — possibly because those inventors need more assistance with protection, commercialization, or management.\n",
        "- This implies that patent count may be predictive of customer status.\n",
        "\n",
        "Blueprinty customers are not selected at random. It may be important to account for systematic differences in the age and regional location of customers vs non-customers."
      ],
      "id": "066652f9"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import seaborn as sns\n",
        "\n",
        "blueprinty = pd.read_csv(\"/home/jovyan/Desktop/mysite/projects/hw2/blueprinty.csv\")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.figure(figsize=(8, 6))\n",
        "sns.boxplot(data=blueprinty, x=\"iscustomer\", y=\"age\")\n",
        "plt.title(\"Age Distribution by Customer Status\")\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"Is Customer (0 = No, 1 = Yes)\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"Age\")\n",
        "plt.xticks([0, 1], [\"Non-Customer\", \"Customer\"])\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()\n",
        "\n",
        "blueprinty.groupby(\"iscustomer\")[\"age\"].describe()\n",
        "\n",
        "region_counts = blueprinty.groupby([\"region\", \"iscustomer\"]).size().reset_index(name=\"count\")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.figure(figsize=(12, 6))\n",
        "sns.barplot(data=region_counts, x=\"region\", y=\"count\", hue=\"iscustomer\")\n",
        "plt.title(\"Customer Status by Region\")\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"Region\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"Count\")\n",
        "plt.legend(title=\"Is Customer\", labels=[\"Non-Customer\", \"Customer\"])\n",
        "plt.xticks(rotation=45)\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "af41cfac",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "🧠 Observations\n",
        "The age distribution of customers and non-customers differs slightly. Boxplots indicate that customers tend to be slightly older, with a higher median age. This could reflect greater experience or longer time in the industry.\n",
        "\n",
        "In terms of region, some areas show a stronger customer presence than others, suggesting regional variation in demand or outreach success. Understanding these patterns could help Blueprinty better target its services geographically.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Estimation of Simple Poisson Model\n",
        "\n",
        "Since our outcome variable of interest can only be small integer values per a set unit of time, we can use a Poisson density to model the number of patents awarded to each engineering firm over the last 5 years. We start by estimating a simple Poisson model via Maximum Likelihood.\n"
      ],
      "id": "ec28b9a7"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "from scipy.special import gammaln\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "\n",
        "blueprinty = pd.read_csv(\"/home/jovyan/Desktop/mysite/projects/hw2/blueprinty.csv\")\n",
        "\n",
        "y_obs = blueprinty[\"patents\"].values\n",
        "\n",
        "def log_likelihood_lambda(lmbda, y):\n",
        "    return np.sum(y * np.log(lmbda) - lmbda - gammaln(y + 1))\n",
        "\n",
        "lambda_vals = np.linspace(0.1, 10, 100)\n",
        "log_likes = [log_likelihood_lambda(lmb, y_obs) for lmb in lambda_vals]\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n",
        "plt.plot(lambda_vals, log_likes, lw=2)\n",
        "plt.title(\"Log-Likelihood of Poisson Model vs. Lambda\")\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"Lambda (λ)\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"Log-Likelihood\")\n",
        "plt.grid(True)\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "0bf5bc52",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import statsmodels.api as sm\n",
        "from scipy.optimize import minimize\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "\n",
        "from scipy.special import gammaln\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "\n",
        "blueprinty = pd.read_csv(\"/home/jovyan/Desktop/mysite/projects/hw2/blueprinty.csv\")\n",
        "\n",
        "def poisson_log_likelihood(beta, X, y):\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    Computes the Poisson log-likelihood given beta, design matrix X, and target y.\n",
        "\n",
        "    Parameters:\n",
        "    - beta: array of coefficients (length p)\n",
        "    - X: design matrix (n x p)\n",
        "    - y: target vector (n,)\n",
        "\n",
        "    Returns:\n",
        "    - negative log-likelihood (to be minimized)\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    lambda_ = np.exp(X @ beta)\n",
        "    log_likelihood = np.sum(y * (X @ beta) - lambda_ - gammaln(y + 1))\n",
        "    return -log_likelihood\n",
        "\n",
        "import statsmodels.api as sm\n",
        "X = blueprinty[[\"age\", \"iscustomer\"]]\n",
        "X = sm.add_constant(X)\n",
        "y = blueprinty[\"patents\"].values\n",
        "\n",
        "beta_init = np.zeros(X.shape[1])\n",
        "\n",
        "poisson_log_likelihood(beta_init, X.values, y)\n",
        "\n",
        "y = blueprinty[\"patents\"].values\n",
        "\n",
        "X = blueprinty[[\"age\", \"iscustomer\"]]\n",
        "X = sm.add_constant(X)\n",
        "X = X.values\n",
        "\n",
        "beta_init = np.zeros(X.shape[1])\n",
        "\n",
        "result = minimize(poisson_log_likelihood, beta_init, args=(X, y), method='BFGS')\n",
        "\n",
        "beta_hat = result.x\n",
        "beta_hat"
      ],
      "id": "6b8239e4",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Estimation of Poisson Regression Model\n",
        "\n",
        "Next, we extend our simple Poisson model to a Poisson Regression Model such that $Y_i = \\text{Poisson}(\\lambda_i)$ where $\\lambda_i = \\exp(X_i'\\beta)$. The interpretation is that the success rate of patent awards is not constant across all firms ($\\lambda$) but rather is a function of firm characteristics $X_i$. Specifically, we will use the covariates age, age squared, region, and whether the firm is a customer of Blueprinty."
      ],
      "id": "dc691faa"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "from scipy.special import gammaln\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import statsmodels.api as sm\n",
        "from scipy.optimize import minimize\n",
        "\n",
        "def poisson_log_likelihood(beta, X, y):\n",
        "    beta = np.asarray(beta)\n",
        "    lambda_ = np.exp(X @ beta)\n",
        "    log_likelihood = np.sum(y * (X @ beta) - lambda_ - gammaln(y + 1))\n",
        "    return -log_likelihood\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "blueprinty = pd.read_csv(\"/home/jovyan/Desktop/mysite/projects/hw2/blueprinty.csv\")\n",
        "blueprinty[\"age2\"] = blueprinty[\"age\"] ** 2\n",
        "X_region = pd.get_dummies(blueprinty[\"region\"], drop_first=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "X = pd.concat([blueprinty[[\"age\", \"age2\", \"iscustomer\"]], X_region], axis=1)\n",
        "X = sm.add_constant(X).values\n",
        "y = blueprinty[\"patents\"].values\n",
        "\n",
        "def poisson_log_likelihood(beta, X, y):\n",
        "    lambda_ = np.exp(X @ beta)\n",
        "    log_likelihood = np.sum(y * (X @ beta) - lambda_ - gammaln(y + 1))\n",
        "    return -log_likelihood\n",
        "\n",
        "beta_init = np.zeros(X.shape[1])\n",
        "result = minimize(poisson_log_likelihood, beta_init, args=(X, y), method=\"BFGS\")\n",
        "\n",
        "beta_hat = result.x\n",
        "beta_hat"
      ],
      "id": "8f792e9f",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "cov_matrix = result.hess_inv\n",
        "standard_errors = np.sqrt(np.diag(cov_matrix))\n",
        "\n",
        "X_columns = [\"const\", \"age\", \"age2\", \"iscustomer\"] + list(X_region.columns)\n",
        "\n",
        "results_df = pd.DataFrame({\n",
        "    \"Coefficient\": result.x,\n",
        "    \"Std. Error\": standard_errors\n",
        "}, index=X_columns)\n",
        "\n",
        "results_df.round(4)"
      ],
      "id": "906ccc72",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "from scipy.special import gammaln\n",
        "from scipy.optimize import minimize\n",
        "import statsmodels.api as sm\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "blueprinty = pd.read_csv(\"/home/jovyan/Desktop/mysite/projects/hw2/blueprinty.csv\")\n",
        "blueprinty[\"age2\"] = blueprinty[\"age\"] ** 2\n",
        "X_region = pd.get_dummies(blueprinty[\"region\"], drop_first=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "X_df = pd.concat([blueprinty[[\"age\", \"age2\", \"iscustomer\"]], X_region], axis=1)\n",
        "X_df = sm.add_constant(X_df)\n",
        "\n",
        "X = X_df.values.astype(np.float64)\n",
        "y = blueprinty[\"patents\"].values.astype(np.float64)\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def poisson_log_likelihood(beta, X, y):\n",
        "    beta = np.atleast_1d(np.asarray(beta, dtype=np.float64))\n",
        "    X = np.asarray(X, dtype=np.float64)\n",
        "    y = np.asarray(y, dtype=np.float64)\n",
        "\n",
        "    lin_pred = X @ beta\n",
        "    lambda_ = np.exp(lin_pred)\n",
        "    log_likelihood = np.sum(y * lin_pred - lambda_ - gammaln(y + 1))\n",
        "    return -log_likelihood\n",
        "\n",
        "beta_init = np.zeros(X.shape[1], dtype=np.float64)\n",
        "result = minimize(poisson_log_likelihood, beta_init, args=(X, y), method=\"BFGS\")\n",
        "beta_hat = result.x\n",
        "\n",
        "cov_matrix = result.hess_inv\n",
        "standard_errors = np.sqrt(np.diag(cov_matrix))\n",
        "\n",
        "results_df = pd.DataFrame({\n",
        "    \"Coefficient\": beta_hat,\n",
        "    \"Std. Error\": standard_errors\n",
        "}, index=X_df.columns)\n",
        "\n",
        "results_df.round(4)\n",
        "\n",
        "glm_model = sm.GLM(y, X, family=sm.families.Poisson()).fit()\n",
        "glm_model.summary2().tables[1].round(4)"
      ],
      "id": "5ec5809e",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## AirBnB Case Study\n",
        "\n",
        "### Introduction\n",
        "\n",
        "AirBnB is a popular platform for booking short-term rentals. In March 2017, students Annika Awad, Evan Lebo, and Anna Linden scraped of 40,000 Airbnb listings from New York City.  The data include the following variables:\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.callout-note collapse=\"true\"}\n",
        "### Variable Definitions\n",
        "\n",
        "    - `id` = unique ID number for each unit\n",
        "    - `last_scraped` = date when information scraped\n",
        "    - `host_since` = date when host first listed the unit on Airbnb\n",
        "    - `days` = `last_scraped` - `host_since` = number of days the unit has been listed\n",
        "    - `room_type` = Entire home/apt., Private room, or Shared room\n",
        "    - `bathrooms` = number of bathrooms\n",
        "    - `bedrooms` = number of bedrooms\n",
        "    - `price` = price per night (dollars)\n",
        "    - `number_of_reviews` = number of reviews for the unit on Airbnb\n",
        "    - `review_scores_cleanliness` = a cleanliness score from reviews (1-10)\n",
        "    - `review_scores_location` = a \"quality of location\" score from reviews (1-10)\n",
        "    - `review_scores_value` = a \"quality of value\" score from reviews (1-10)\n",
        "    - `instant_bookable` = \"t\" if instantly bookable, \"f\" if not\n",
        "\n",
        "::::"
      ],
      "id": "7e78939e"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "airbnb = pd.read_csv(\"/home/jovyan/Desktop/mysite/projects/hw2/airbnb.csv\")\n",
        "\n",
        "airbnb_clean = airbnb[[\n",
        "    \"number_of_reviews\", \"price\", \"days\", \"review_scores_cleanliness\",\n",
        "    \"review_scores_location\", \"review_scores_value\", \"instant_bookable\"\n",
        "]].dropna()\n",
        "\n",
        "airbnb_clean[\"instant_bookable\"] = airbnb_clean[\"instant_bookable\"].map({\"t\": 1, \"f\": 0})\n",
        "\n",
        "import seaborn as sns\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.figure(figsize=(8, 5))\n",
        "sns.histplot(airbnb_clean[\"number_of_reviews\"], bins=40)\n",
        "plt.title(\"Distribution of Number of Reviews\")\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"Number of Reviews\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"Count\")\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "18cc12ee",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    }
